    <bpmn:process id="W_W567" name="W567. Employee Cross-Training &amp; Skill Matrix Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New department assignment; quarterly skill assessment cycle; new product category launch; staffing gap requiring cross-trained coverage
Frequency: Quarterly skill assessments for all 6,911 employees; continuous cross-training assignments (~1,500–2,000 per quarter)
Volume: Higher during new store openings (cross-training for new departments) and seasonal peaks
Owner: Training Manager / Store Manager (store-level execution)
Participants: Training Manager, Department Supervisor (R for training execution), Employee, Store Manager (A for assignment), HR Business Partner (I)
Source: workflow W567 — Employee Cross-Training &amp; Skill Matrix Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W567_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W567_Lane1" name="Training Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W567_Lane2" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W567_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W567_Lane4" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W567_Lane5" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W567_End20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W567_Start7" name="New department assignment; quarterly skill assessment cycle; new product category launch…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task8" name="Training Manager establishes skill matrix template per department: (a) product…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Training Manager establishes skill matrix template per department: (a) product knowledge levels — beginner (top 20 SKUs, basic features), intermediate (top 50 SKUs, customer scenarios, compatibility), advanced (full catalog, technical specifications, project consultation); (b) POS operations — basic (scan, tender, void) and advanced (special orders, returns, layaway); (c) safety procedures — department-specific hazards and PPE requirements; (d) specialized services — paint mixing, lumber cutting, pipe threading, tile cutting, electrical testing; template configured in ERP skill matrix module
Responsible (R): Training Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 days (initial setup); 1 day/quarter review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task9" name="Initial skill assessment: Department Supervisor evaluates each associate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Initial skill assessment: Department Supervisor evaluates each associate against the skill matrix for their assigned department using structured assessment form — product knowledge quiz (top 20 SKUs by sales value), POS proficiency test, safety procedure walkthrough; results recorded in ERP with assessor ID and date; self-assessment component (employee rates own confidence per skill area) included for gap comparison
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Training Manager
Duration: 30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W567_Task10" name="Gap analysis: system identifies departments where cross-coverage is weakest —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Gap analysis: system identifies departments where cross-coverage is weakest — minimum coverage threshold: 2 associates per department with intermediate-level product knowledge; system generates cross-coverage heatmap per store showing departments below threshold in red, at threshold in amber, above in green; identifies individual employees whose skill gaps limit their cross-department utility
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task11" name="Cross-training plan creation: Training Manager generates quarterly training…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-training plan creation: Training Manager generates quarterly training calendar with rotation assignments based on gap analysis — priority: (a) departments below minimum coverage threshold; (b) employees with narrow skill sets (competent in only 1 department); (c) new product category launches requiring new skills; each cross-training assignment targets 1 new department per associate per quarter
Responsible (R): Training Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task12" name="Cross-training execution: assigned associate shadows experienced associate in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cross-training execution: assigned associate shadows experienced associate in target department for 2–4 hour sessions (minimum 3 sessions per department); session 1: department orientation — layout, top 20 SKUs, customer personas, common questions; session 2: hands-on — assist customers under supervision, practice POS transactions for department-specific items; session 3: assessment preparation — review product guide, practice customer scenarios, safety procedures
Responsible (R): Employee / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/session × 3 sessions = 6–12 hours/department</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task13" name="Practical assessment: target department&#x27;s Department Supervisor tests…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Practical assessment: target department&#x27;s Department Supervisor tests cross-trainee on: (a) top 20 SKUs — identify product, explain key features, suggest alternatives; (b) 3 basic customer scenarios — assist customer with product selection, handle return/exchange, process special order; (c) safety procedures — department-specific hazards, PPE requirements, emergency procedures; pass threshold: 70% correct; if failed, 1 additional shadow session + re-assessment within 2 weeks
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Training Manager
Duration: 30–45 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W567_Task14" name="Skill matrix update in ERP: system records certification date, skill level…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Skill matrix update in ERP: system records certification date, skill level (beginner/intermediate/advanced) per department per employee, assessor ID, assessment score; cross-coverage heatmap auto-refreshes; store-level skill matrix dashboard updated for Store Manager visibility
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task15" name="Store Manager reviews cross-coverage heatmap — identifies departments still…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Store Manager reviews cross-coverage heatmap — identifies departments still below minimum coverage threshold; escalates persistent gaps (&gt;2 consecutive quarters below threshold) to Training Manager for targeted intervention; approves or modifies shift assignments to leverage cross-trained associates
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Training Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W567_Task16" name="Scheduling integration: W34 shift scheduling prioritizes cross-trained…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Scheduling integration: W34 shift scheduling prioritizes cross-trained associates for coverage during absences — when associate calls in sick, system suggests cross-trained replacement from another department; during peak periods (weekends, payday, seasonal rush), Store Manager assigns cross-trained associates to high-traffic departments; scheduling system flags departments at risk of no cross-coverage in upcoming schedule
Responsible (R): Store Manager / System
Accountable (A): Training Manager
Duration: Absorbed in W34 scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task17" name="Recognition and development: top cross-trained associates (certified in 3+…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Recognition and development: top cross-trained associates (certified in 3+ departments at intermediate level) identified for: (a) recognition per W72 performance management — cross-training achievement as performance differentiator; (b) potential promotion to Department Supervisor or to senior Sales Associate roles; (c) management trainee program candidate identification per W179; (d) higher-priority consideration for preferred shift assignments
Responsible (R): Training Manager / HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Absorbed in W72 cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W567_Task18" name="Quarterly re-assessment: system tracks certification age — certifications older…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Quarterly re-assessment: system tracks certification age — certifications older than 6 months without practice (no shifts worked in certified department) flagged for re-assessment; skill decay mitigation: associates assigned to work at least 1 shift per quarter in each cross-trained department to maintain certification; expired certifications downgraded to beginner level pending re-assessment
Responsible (R): System / Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Training Manager
Duration: 15 min/employee (re-assessment)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W567_Task19" name="Annual skill matrix review: Training Manager aggregates cross-training data for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Annual skill matrix review: Training Manager aggregates cross-training data for annual talent review — feeds into W178 (succession planning — cross-trained associates as internal mobility candidates) and W179 (management trainee — high-performing cross-trained associates identified as program candidates); annual report to COO: cross-coverage by store, certification rates, training hours invested, turnover impact analysis
Responsible (R): Training Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W567_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W567_End20" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W567_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W567_Annotation21">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: focusing cross-training on beginner-to-intermediate levels; operational: scheduling cross-training during lower-traffic periods (weekday mornings); operational: quarterly minimum-shift requirement and re-assessment protocol
Owner: Training Manager / Store Manager (store-level execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W567_Assoc22" sourceRef="W567_Annotation21" targetRef="W567_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W567_Flow23" sourceRef="W567_Start7" targetRef="W567_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W567_Flow24" sourceRef="W567_Task8" targetRef="W567_Task9" />
