    <bpmn:process id="W_W956" name="W956. Employee Annual Physical Examination &amp; Occupational Health Clearance Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee reaches annual physical examination (APE) due date (employment anniversary or birth month, depending on company policy)
Frequency: ~576 employees/month (6,911 ÷ 12)
Volume: 1 employee per examination event
Owner: HR Manager
Participants: Employee, HR Assistant, Accredited Clinic/Hospital, Payroll Officer, Store Manager/Department Head, Occupational Health Nurse
Source: workflow W956 — Employee Annual Physical Examination &amp; Occupational Health Clearance Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W956_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W956_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W956_Lane2" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W956_Lane3" name="Clinic">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W956_Lane4" name="HR Assistant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W956_Lane5" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W956_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W956_Start7" name="Employee reaches annual physical examination (APE) due date (employment anniversary or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W956_Task8" name="Annual Schedule Generation &amp; Notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual Schedule Generation &amp; Notification: System generates annual APE schedule per entity: (a) employee birth month grouping (standard Philippine practice); (b) new hires: APE within 30 days of onboarding per W15; (c) system sends notification 30 days before due date: (i) employee email/app notification — scheduled date, accredited clinic list, fasting requirements, required tests based on role; (ii) Store Manager/Department Head — list of employees due for APE; (iii) HR Assistant — master schedule and tracking dashboard; (d) employee selects preferred accredited clinic from panel (3–5 clinics per region, negotiated rates per corporate partnership per W149)
Responsible (R): System / HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: Automated + 2 hours/month scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W956_Task9" name="Pre-Examination Requirements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pre-Examination Requirements: Employee prepares: (a) APE authorization letter from BuildRight (system-generated, with employee name, entity, and approved test package); (b) valid company ID; (c) 10–12 hour fasting (for blood tests); (d) for hazmat-exposed employees: additional occupational health assessment form completed by Department Supervisor documenting exposure history; (e) employee visits accredited clinic on scheduled date; walk-in accepted with authorization letter (no appointment required at accredited clinics)
Responsible (R): Employee
Accountable (A): Department Head
Duration: 30 min (employee preparation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W956_Task10" name="Examination &amp; Results Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Examination &amp; Results Processing: Clinic conducts examination: (a) standard package: physical exam, CBC, urinalysis, chest X-ray, visual acuity, drug test; (b) hazmat package (add): liver function test, kidney function test, pulmonary function test; (c) driver package (add): visual acuity (corrected 20/40 minimum), hearing test, reflex test per W654; (d) clinic releases results to: (i) employee — personal copy with physician&#x27;s notes; (ii) BuildRight HR — occupational health clearance summary (fit/unfit/restricted) via secure portal per RA 10173; clinic does NOT share specific medical diagnoses with BuildRight — only fitness-for-duty assessment
Responsible (R): Clinic / Employee
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours (employee at clinic)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W956_Task11" name="Clearance Processing &amp; Work Restriction Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Clearance Processing &amp; Work Restriction Management: HR processes clearance: (a) fit for duty → no action, clearance recorded in employee health file, APE completion noted in HR system; (b) fit with restrictions → HR coordinates with Department Head: (i) restrictions documented (e.g., &quot;no heavy lifting &gt; 10kg for 30 days,&quot; &quot;no exposure to respiratory irritants&quot;); (ii) work accommodation implemented (reassignment to lighter duties, temporary restriction from hazmat areas); (iii) follow-up examination scheduled per physician recommendation; (c) unfit for duty → HR initiates: (i) medical leave per company policy and SSS sickness benefit; (ii) extended medical evaluation at company expense; (iii) return-to-work clearance required per W805 before resuming duties; (d) drug test positive → per W483 Drug-Free Workplace protocol: confirmed positive leads to mandatory rehabilitation (first offense) or termination (second offense) per company policy and DOLE due process per W603
Responsible (R): HR Assistant / Occupational Health Nurse
Accountable (A): HR Manager / Department Head
Duration: 15–30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W956_Task12" name="Compliance Reporting &amp; Analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Compliance Reporting &amp; Analytics: (a) monthly: HR tracks APE completion rate per entity, store, and department; targets 100% compliance within birth month + 30-day grace period; overdue employees escalated to Department Head; (b) quarterly: aggregate health statistics (no individual data) reported to CHRO: completion rate, restriction rate, common restrictions by department, clinic satisfaction; (c) annual: DOLE OSH compliance report per W436 includes APE completion certification; (d) annual: clinic panel review per W149 — clinic quality, turnaround time, pricing, and employee satisfaction; clinic accreditation renewed or changed based on performance
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Occupational Health Nurse
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W956_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W956_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W956_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W956_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: 100% APE completion required for DOLE compliance per W436; operational: confirmatory testing (GC-MS) required before action per W483
Owner: HR Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W956_Assoc15" sourceRef="W956_Annotation14" targetRef="W956_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow16" sourceRef="W956_Start7" targetRef="W956_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow17" sourceRef="W956_Task8" targetRef="W956_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow18" sourceRef="W956_Task9" targetRef="W956_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow19" sourceRef="W956_Task10" targetRef="W956_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow20" sourceRef="W956_Task11" targetRef="W956_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W956_Flow21" sourceRef="W956_Task12" targetRef="W956_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W956_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W956_plane" bpmnElement="W_W956">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W956_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W956_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W956_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W956_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
