    <bpmn:process id="W_W957" name="W957. Employee Tuition Assistance &amp; Educational Advancement Program Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee applies for tuition assistance or educational leave via HR self-service portal
Frequency: ~80–120 applications/year
Volume: 1 course/degree per application; average assistance PHP 15,000–30,000/semester
Owner: HR Manager
Participants: Employee, Department Head, HR Manager, CHRO, Finance (payroll), Academic Institution
Source: workflow W957 — Employee Tuition Assistance &amp; Educational Advancement Program Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W957_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W957_Lane1" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W957_Lane2" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W957_Lane3" name="HR Assistant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W957_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W957_Start5" name="Employee applies for tuition assistance or educational leave via HR self-service portal">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W957_Task6" name="Application &amp; Eligibility Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Application &amp; Eligibility Verification: Employee submits application via HR self-service portal: (a) personal information, current role, entity, and length of service; (b) intended course/degree, institution, and expected completion date; (c) estimated tuition cost per semester; (d) justification: how the program relates to current role or career development at BuildRight; (e) HR verifies eligibility: (i) minimum 1 year of service; (ii) performance rating ≥ &quot;Meets Expectations&quot; per W72; (iii) no active disciplinary actions per W603; (iv) course must be from CHED-recognized institution (degrees) or TESDA-accredited training center (vocational); (v) priority given to programs aligned with BuildRight&#x27;s strategic skill needs per W645
Responsible (R): Employee / HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 15–20 min (employee) + 15 min (HR)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W957_Task7" name="Approval &amp; Agreement Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Approval &amp; Agreement Execution: (a) HR Manager reviews application: eligibility, course relevance, budget availability (annual TAP budget: PHP 3–5M); (b) for assistance ≤ PHP 30,000/year: HR Manager approves; for &gt; PHP 30,000/year: CHRO approves; (c) approved employee signs Educational Assistance Agreement: (i) assistance amount and disbursement schedule (per semester); (ii) grade requirement: minimum &quot;passing&quot; for all funded subjects; grade below passing → employee reimburses BuildRight for that subject&#x27;s cost; (iii) service obligation: employee must remain employed for 12 months after last disbursement per semester funded; early resignation → pro-rated reimbursement of assistance; (iv) tax treatment: educational assistance is a taxable benefit per BIR (subject to 13th month pay threshold rules) unless qualified as de minimis benefit per BIR Revenue Regulations; Finance advises on tax treatment per application
Responsible (R): HR Manager / CHRO / Employee
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W957_Task8" name="Disbursement &amp; Enrollment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Disbursement &amp; Enrollment: (a) HR processes disbursement per semester: (i) payment directly to institution (preferred) via AP per W7; or (ii) reimbursement to employee upon presentation of official enrollment receipt and assessment; (b) system records disbursement in employee TAP account; (c) for educational leave: HR coordinates schedule adjustment with Department Head per W561 — employee may receive reduced work hours (e.g., 6-hour workdays) or shift reassignment to accommodate class schedule; (d) Payroll adjusts: tax withholding for taxable benefit amount per W10
Responsible (R): HR Assistant / Finance
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 30 min/semester</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W957_Task9" name="Academic Progress Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Academic Progress Monitoring: (a) employee submits grade report at end of each semester/term within 30 days of release; (b) HR verifies: (i) all funded subjects passed → assistance continues; (ii) any funded subject failed → employee must reimburse cost of failed subject within 60 days (payroll deduction per W76 loan module); (iii) employee withdrawn from program → service obligation clock starts; full assistance amount becomes repayable if employee resigns before 12-month service obligation; (c) employee updates: expected graduation date, any change in program or institution; (d) HR tracks program completion rate and average GPA per TAP cohort
Responsible (R): Employee / HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 15 min/semester</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W957_Task10" name="Completion &amp; Talent Integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Completion &amp; Talent Integration: (a) employee graduates/completes certification: submits diploma/certificate to HR; (b) HR records completion in talent profile per W178 succession management; (c) HR discusses career advancement opportunities: (i) internal job posting for relevant open positions per W682; (ii) promotion consideration at next performance review cycle per W72; (iii) management trainee program (W179) if applicable; (d) system removes service obligation flag after 12-month post-disbursement period; (e) annual: CHRO reviews TAP ROI — completion rate, internal promotion rate of TAP graduates, retention rate vs. non-TAP employees, cost-per-promoted-employee
Responsible (R): HR Manager / Employee
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30 min/completion</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W957_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W957_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W957_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W957_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: HR Manager review and approval gate
Owner: HR Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W957_Assoc13" sourceRef="W957_Annotation12" targetRef="W957_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow14" sourceRef="W957_Start5" targetRef="W957_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow15" sourceRef="W957_Task6" targetRef="W957_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow16" sourceRef="W957_Task7" targetRef="W957_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow17" sourceRef="W957_Task8" targetRef="W957_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow18" sourceRef="W957_Task9" targetRef="W957_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W957_Flow19" sourceRef="W957_Task10" targetRef="W957_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
