    <bpmn:process id="W_W1001" name="W1001. Store-Level Employee Performance-Based Profit Sharing &amp; Incentive Bonus Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly/quarterly store performance review cycle; achievement of profit sharing or bonus thresholds
Frequency: Monthly calculation; quarterly payout
Volume: All store employees (~29 per store × 200 stores = ~5,800 employees)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, HR Department, Finance Department, CHRO
Source: workflow W1001 — Store-Level Employee Performance-Based Profit Sharing &amp; Incentive Bonus Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1001_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1001_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1001_Lane2" name="HR Department">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1001_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1001_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1001_Start5" name="Monthly/quarterly store performance review cycle; achievement of profit sharing or bonus…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1001_Task6" name="Monthly Store Performance Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly Store Performance Calculation: System calculates store-level performance: (a) actual sales vs. target sales (per store budget per W26); (b) actual gross margin vs. target gross margin (28–32% target); (c) store operating expenses vs. budget (labor cost, utilities, supplies); (d) shrinkage/loss rate vs. target (&lt;1.5% of sales); (e) customer satisfaction score vs. target (≥85%); (f) net store profit vs. target; (g) system calculates profit sharing pool = 10% of store profit above target (if store exceeds target); maximum pool capped at 20% of store payroll; (h) if store does not exceed target: no profit sharing pool for that quarter
Responsible (R): System / Finance Department
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1001_Task7" name="Individual Performance Scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Individual Performance Scoring: System calculates individual employee scores based on: (a) attendance and punctuality (biometric data per W34) — weight 15%; (b) sales contribution (individual sales per POS login for Sales Associates, or department sales for Department Supervisors) — weight 25%; (c) customer satisfaction (individual CSAT scores from post-transaction surveys) — weight 20%; (d) shrinkage in assigned area (cycle count variance per W6) — weight 15%; (e) training completion (certifications per W51) — weight 10%; (f) peer and manager evaluation (Store Manager and Department Supervisor subjective assessment) — weight 15%; (g) individual score = weighted average of all components, normalized to 0–100 scale
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/quarter per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1001_Task8" name="Profit Sharing Distribution Calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Profit Sharing Distribution Calculation: System calculates individual payout: (a) employee share = profit sharing pool × (individual score ÷ sum of all employee scores in store); (b) pro-rata adjustment for employees with &lt;3 months tenure or partial-quarter employment; (c) minimum payout threshold — employee must score ≥60/100 to receive any payout; (d) maximum individual payout capped at 1.5× monthly basic salary per quarter (DOLE compliance — ensures bonus remains discretionary and not structurally guaranteed); (e) Store Manager reviews distribution and approves; (f) Finance Department validates calculation and approves total pool
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager / Finance Department
Accountable (A): CHRO (policy), Finance Department (budget)
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1001_Task9" name="Payout Processing &amp; Communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payout Processing &amp; Communication: HR processes payout: (a) profit sharing amount added to employee&#x27;s regular semi-monthly payroll per W10 as a separate line item &quot;Quarterly Profit Share&quot;; (b) tax treatment — profit sharing is taxable compensation income per BIR (not tax-exempt); employer withholding tax per TRAIN law graduated table per W90; (c) profit sharing does NOT count toward 13th month pay calculation (per DOLE advisory, discretionary bonuses are excluded from 13th month base); (d) Store Manager conducts individual or team meeting to communicate: payout amount, performance score breakdown, and areas for improvement; (e) system generates individual performance statement showing score components and payout
Responsible (R): HR Department / Finance Department / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per payout cycle (team meeting)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1001_Task10" name="Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Goal Setting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly Performance Review &amp; Goal Setting: Store Manager conducts quarterly performance review with each employee: (a) reviews individual score breakdown — strengths, areas for improvement; (b) discusses customer feedback and shrinkage data; (c) sets specific goals for next quarter (e.g., increase individual sales by 10%, complete product knowledge certification per W51, improve attendance); (d) identifies training needs per W51; (e) documents goals in performance management system per W72; (f) for underperformers (score &lt;60): Store Manager implements performance improvement plan per W72 with 30-day review cycle
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 15–20 min per employee (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1001_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1001_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1001_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1001_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1001_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1001_Annotation12" targetRef="W1001_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow14" sourceRef="W1001_Start5" targetRef="W1001_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow15" sourceRef="W1001_Task6" targetRef="W1001_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow16" sourceRef="W1001_Task7" targetRef="W1001_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow17" sourceRef="W1001_Task8" targetRef="W1001_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow18" sourceRef="W1001_Task9" targetRef="W1001_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1001_Flow19" sourceRef="W1001_Task10" targetRef="W1001_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1001_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1001_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1001">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1001_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1001_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
