    <bpmn:process id="W_W1042" name="W1042. Employee Store-Level Rotational Cross-Training &amp; Multi-Skill Certification Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New employee onboarding (W15); annual skill assessment cycle; operational need for multi-skilled workforce
Frequency: Continuous program; each employee rotates through 2–3 departments over 6–12 months
Volume: ~5,800 store employees; ~1,200–1,600 new hires/year; all existing store staff participate in rotational cross-training
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Department Supervisors, Employee, HR Training Coordinator, District Manager (oversight)
Source: workflow W1042 — Employee Store-Level Rotational Cross-Training &amp; Multi-Skill Certification Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1042_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1042_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1042_Lane2" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1042_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1042_Lane4" name="HR Training Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1042_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1042_Start6" name="New employee onboarding (W15); annual skill assessment cycle; operational need for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1042_Task7" name="Cross-Training Plan Assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Cross-Training Plan Assignment: For each employee (new hire or existing): (a) Store Manager assigns a cross-training plan based on: (i) employee&#x27;s primary department, (ii) store&#x27;s coverage gaps (which departments are understaffed or have single-point-of-failure), (iii) employee&#x27;s interests and aptitude (assessed during onboarding per W609 for new hires or performance review per W72 for existing staff); (b) standard cross-training paths: (i) Sales Associate (Tools/Hardware) → cross-train in Lumber &amp; Building Materials + Plumbing/Electrical (high-demand departments); (ii) Cashier → cross-train in Customer Service + Stock Associate (flexible floor coverage); (iii) Stock Associate → cross-train in Receiving Clerk + Paint Mixing Station (W1003); (iv) Customer Service Rep → cross-train in Cashiering + Pro Desk (W112); (c) each employee is assigned a &quot;home department&quot; (primary) and 1–2 &quot;cross-trained departments&quot;; (d) target: within 12 months of hire, every Sales Associate is certified in at least 1 additional department; every support staff is certified in at least 1 alternative support role
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Department Supervisors
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per employee (initial plan)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1042_Task8" name="Department Rotation &amp; On-the-Job Training">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Department Rotation &amp; On-the-Job Training: Employee rotates through cross-training department(s): (a) rotation schedule: employee spends 1 full day per week (or 2 half-days) in the cross-training department for 8–12 weeks; (b) during rotation: (i) assigned a &quot;buddy&quot; from the cross-training department (experienced Sales Associate or Supervisor) per W609 (Buddy System); (ii) buddy provides hands-on training: product knowledge (top 50 SKUs in the department), customer interaction techniques, department-specific procedures (e.g., paint mixing per W1003, lumber cutting per W169, tile quantity estimation per W963); (iii) employee shadows buddy for first rotation, then handles customer interactions under buddy supervision for subsequent rotations; (c) rotation schedule coordinated by Store Manager to ensure both the home department and cross-training department are adequately staffed during rotation days; (d) Store Manager ensures rotation is meaningful (employee actively learning, not just standing around) by providing a rotation checklist with specific skills to observe and practice
Responsible (R): Employee / Buddy (Peer Trainer)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 days over 8–12 weeks (1 day/week)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1042_Task9" name="Skill Assessment &amp; Certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Skill Assessment &amp; Certification: After 8–12 weeks of rotation: (a) Department Supervisor of the cross-training department assesses employee&#x27;s competency: (i) product knowledge quiz (minimum 80% pass): identify top 50 SKUs, describe key features, recommend correct product for common customer scenarios; (ii) practical assessment: employee handles 3–5 customer interactions in the cross-training department under Supervisor observation — rated on product knowledge accuracy, customer interaction quality, and process compliance; (iii) procedure assessment: employee demonstrates department-specific procedures (e.g., paint mixing station operation, lumber yard safety, tile gallery customer guidance); (b) assessment results recorded in skill matrix system per W567; (c) Certified: employee passes all assessments → certified in cross-training department, eligible for deployment; (d) Not Yet Certified: employee needs additional rotation (4–8 more weeks) → continue training; (e) certification valid for 12 months; recertification required annually through refresher rotation (1 day) and updated product knowledge quiz
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min per employee assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1042_Task10" name="Deployment &amp; Scheduling Integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Deployment &amp; Scheduling Integration: Certified cross-trained employees are deployed flexibly: (a) Store Manager uses cross-training certification status in weekly shift scheduling per W34: (i) each shift must have at least 1 certified person per department; (ii) if primary department associate is absent, cross-trained associate from another department is scheduled to cover; (b) during peak periods (payday weekends, bi-monthly sales): Store Manager deploys cross-trained staff to high-traffic departments regardless of their home department; (c) cross-trained employees receive a &quot;Multi-Skill&quot; badge on their employee profile in the system — visible to Store Manager and DM during scheduling and performance reviews; (d) cross-training status factored into employee performance review per W72: demonstrated multi-skilled capability is a positive factor for promotion consideration
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): District Manager
Duration: Integrated into W34 scheduling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1042_Task11" name="Program Effectiveness Tracking &amp; Continuous Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Program Effectiveness Tracking &amp; Continuous Improvement: (a) HR Training Coordinator tracks program metrics per store per W567: (i) cross-training certification rate: % of store staff certified in at least 1 additional department (target: 80% within 12 months of hire), (ii) average time to certification, (iii) certification pass rate on first attempt, (iv) deployment utilization: how often cross-trained staff are actually deployed to secondary departments; (b) Store Manager feedback: does cross-training reduce overtime per W1032? reduce stockouts from uncovered departments? improve customer satisfaction per W608?; (c) DM benchmarking per W1030: compare cross-training rates across stores — identify best practices from high-performing stores; (d) quarterly: HR Training Coordinator updates cross-training curriculum based on: (i) new product launches per W564 (updated product knowledge quiz), (ii) process changes (new procedures added to practical assessment), (iii) store-specific needs (stores near construction boom areas may need more Plumbing/Electrical cross-training); (e) annual: program review by CHRO and COO — adjust targets, training methods, and incentives based on program ROI
Responsible (R): HR Training Coordinator / Store Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter (HR) + 1 hour/month (Store Manager)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1042_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1042_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1042_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1042_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: (W34) must incorporate cross-training status as a constraint in its optimization algorithm
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1042_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1042_Annotation13" targetRef="W1042_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow15" sourceRef="W1042_Start6" targetRef="W1042_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow16" sourceRef="W1042_Task7" targetRef="W1042_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow17" sourceRef="W1042_Task8" targetRef="W1042_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow18" sourceRef="W1042_Task9" targetRef="W1042_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow19" sourceRef="W1042_Task10" targetRef="W1042_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1042_Flow20" sourceRef="W1042_Task11" targetRef="W1042_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1042_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1042_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1042">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1042_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1042_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="72" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1042_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1042_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1042_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1042_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1042_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
