    <bpmn:process id="W_W1127" name="W1127. Store-Level Employee Annual Competency Re-Certification &amp; Skills Refresher" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual re-certification cycle (employee&#x27;s hire anniversary month), or regulatory requirement renewal, or new product/equipment introduction
Frequency: ~5,900 re-certifications/year (6,911 employees × ~85% requiring annual refresh, spread across 12 months)
Volume: 1–4 competency modules per employee per cycle
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Sales Associate / Cashier / Stock Associate, HR Training Coordinator
Source: workflow W1127 — Store-Level Employee Annual Competency Re-Certification &amp; Skills Refresher</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1127_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1127_Lane1" name="HR System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1127_Lane2" name="Employee">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1127_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1127_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1127_Start5" name="Annual re-certification cycle (employee&#x27;s hire anniversary month), or regulatory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1127_Task6" name="Annual Re-Certification Schedule Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Annual Re-Certification Schedule Generation: (a) HR system generates annual re-certification schedule by employee based on hire date anniversary; (b) each employee assigned 1–4 competency modules based on role: Cashier = POS proficiency + cash handling + BIR compliance + customer service; Sales Associate = product knowledge (department-specific) + customer service + returns processing; Receiving Clerk = goods receipt + inventory management + safety + forklift (if certified); Stock Associate = inventory management + safety + equipment operation; (c) schedule distributed to Department Supervisors 30 days before re-certification month
Responsible (R): HR System / HR Training Coordinator
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1127_Task7" name="Self-Study Module Completion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Self-Study Module Completion: (a) employee accesses assigned e-learning modules via mobile app or store backroom tablet; (b) modules include: updated product catalog for assigned department, new POS features and procedure changes, safety refresher (hazmat, emergency, ergonomics), regulatory updates (BIR, DTI, DOLE changes); (c) average module length: 30–45 minutes; (d) employee completes modules during scheduled downtime (before store opening, after closing, or slow periods with supervisor approval); (e) system tracks module completion progress and sends reminders
Responsible (R): Employee
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30–45 min/module</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1127_Task8" name="Practical Skills Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Practical Skills Assessment: (a) Department Supervisor conducts hands-on assessment for each competency module: POS — process sample transactions including returns, discounts, loyalty enrollment, split tender; product knowledge — identify products, explain features, recommend complementary items; safety — demonstrate PPE usage, emergency procedure walkthrough, hazmat spill response; equipment — demonstrate safe operation of assigned equipment; (b) assessment scored using standardized rubric in ERP; (c) passing threshold: 80% for POS/cash handling, 70% for product knowledge, 100% for safety-critical items; (d) results recorded in employee&#x27;s digital training record
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 15–30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1127_Task9" name="Remedial Training &amp; Re-Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Remedial Training &amp; Re-Assessment: (a) employees scoring below threshold on any module receive targeted remedial coaching from Department Supervisor or designated trainer; (b) remedial training completed within 14 days; (c) re-assessment scheduled; (d) if employee fails re-assessment: formal performance coaching initiated per W72 (employee performance management), with extended training plan; (e) for safety-critical competencies (forklift, hazmat): employee restricted from related duties until certified; (f) HR notified of all failed re-certifications for trend analysis
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / HR Training Coordinator
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1127_Task10" name="Certification Record Update &amp; Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Certification Record Update &amp; Reporting: (a) successful completions update employee&#x27;s digital certification record in HR module; (b) certification status visible to Store Manager and HR; (c) system flags employees with lapsed certifications (not completed within anniversary month + 30-day grace period); (d) quarterly compliance report generated: re-certification completion rate by store, region, and competency domain; (e) data feeds into performance review (W72) and skills matrix (W567)
Responsible (R): HR System
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1127_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1127_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1127_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1127_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: Department Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1127_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1127_Annotation12" targetRef="W1127_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow14" sourceRef="W1127_Start5" targetRef="W1127_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow15" sourceRef="W1127_Task6" targetRef="W1127_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow16" sourceRef="W1127_Task7" targetRef="W1127_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow17" sourceRef="W1127_Task8" targetRef="W1127_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow18" sourceRef="W1127_Task9" targetRef="W1127_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1127_Flow19" sourceRef="W1127_Task10" targetRef="W1127_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1127_diag">
