    <bpmn:process id="W_W5527" name="W5527. Leadership Development &amp; Management-Capability Program (HiPo Development)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: High-potential identification from the annual succession review (W178); a leadership-pipeline gap from W3345 workforce planning; a first-time-manager promotion event; the annual program-enrollment cycle; or program-effectiveness review findings
Frequency: Annual enrollment cycle aligned to the W178 talent review; per-promotion event; quarterly cohort sessions; annual program review
Volume: ~230 succession-critical roles (200 Store Managers + 30 Department Head/Manager roles); ~60–80 HiPo/leadership candidates/year; ~25–35 first-time-manager promotions/year
Owner: CHRO
Participants: HR Manager, HR Business Partners, Department Heads, Regional Managers (store-cohort sponsors), external leadership-program &amp; coaching providers, LMS Administrator
Source: workflow W5527 — Leadership Development &amp; Management-Capability Program (HiPo Development)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5527_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5527_Lane1" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5527_Lane2" name="HR Business Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5527_Lane3" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5527_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5527_Start5" name="High-potential identification from the annual succession review (W178); a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task6" name="Program design &amp; competency model">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Program design &amp; competency model: maintain the leadership competency framework across the store-leadership and HQ-people-leadership tracks, aligned to the W3306 career framework and the W72 performance dimensions; refresh annually
Responsible (R): CHRO / HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task7" name="Enrollment &amp; nomination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Enrollment &amp; nomination: candidates nominated from W178 succession slates, W3345 pipeline gaps and W3778 cadet-program graduates; HR Business Partners validate nominations with Department Heads
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 30 min/candidate × ~70/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task8" name="Cohort delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cohort delivery: quarterly leadership modules blending external providers and internal leaders — financial acumen co-delivered with FP&amp;A (W1405 store-P&amp;L), conflict &amp; labor-relations basics with the VS-84 discipline, safety leadership with the Safety Officer
Responsible (R): HR Manager / external providers
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 8 hours/session × 12 sessions/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task9" name="First-time-manager transition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: First-time-manager transition: promotion-triggered onboarding covering delegation basics, scheduling and labor compliance (W34/W1032), and performance conversations (W72); mentor assignment pairing each participant with an experienced Store Manager
Responsible (R): HR Business Partner / Store Manager
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 4 hours/participant × ~30/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task10" name="Progress &amp; development-plan tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Progress &amp; development-plan tracking: 360-feedback cycle, individual development plans and stretch-assignment log maintained in the HRIS; progression data feeds the next W178 review
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2 hours/candidate × ~70/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5527_Task11" name="Program review &amp; effectiveness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Program review &amp; effectiveness: annual review of internal-promotion rate, 90-day new-manager retention and engagement deltas (W3338 survey feeds); curriculum and provider adjustments
Responsible (R): CHRO / HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 8 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5527_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5527_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5527_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5527_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-299 (ensure controlled execution — Learning &amp; Development (PA-19.4).) | - operational: enrollment requires a W178-slate or W3345-gap justification | - operational: annual program review presented to the executive committee
Owner: CHRO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
